== Includes ==
Use a Domain when the field is a recurring, stable knowledge surface with enough corpus/navigation need to justify explicit semantic identity, a category, a portal, and at least one real exemplar.

== Excludes / boundary ==
This is '''not an exhaustive metaphysical taxonomy of all knowledge'''. Subfields such as Python or Bioinformatics may have categories and portals without becoming top-level Domains. Project administration, maintenance, epistemics, lifecycle, Entity type, and Book Matter are separate dimensions.

== Category role ==
'''Controlled semantic-vocabulary index + navigation root.''' Category hierarchy does not itself assign the `Domain` property; semantic identity remains explicit on each knowledge object.

== Expansion rule ==
Add Domains from demonstrated corpus/coverage need, not because a fashionable topic exists. Current research candidates include Earth/environmental science, information/knowledge science, psychology/cognitive science, social sciences, history, geography, linguistics, law/governance, education, agriculture/food systems, astronomy/space science, and materials science.

See [[BITwiki:Navigation and coverage research]], [[BITwiki:Organization]], and [[BITwiki:Research references]].
